## Flags for the daemon's VM: `bin/troupe_daemon start`, and the `eval` behind every other
## `troupe-daemon` command. A release is built on the platform it runs on.
<%= if match?({:win32, _}, :os.type()) do %>
## Windows (#231, root Decision 719). The VM shares a console, the one `troupe-daemon run`
## was typed in or the one `troupe daemon run` runs in, and reads none of it.
##
## -noinput: no reader on the console. Nothing here reads standard input.
## +Bc: Ctrl-C is not the break handler's. The wrapper gives this VM the null device for
## standard input (`bin/troupe-daemon.cmd`), so +Bc leaves the console's mode alone, Ctrl-C
## stays the signal it is at a prompt, and it ends this VM at once, with no menu to answer.
-noinput
+Bc
<% end %>
